<title>USA: Time Warner swaps Wisconsin cable operations.</title>
<headline>Time Warner swaps Wisconsin cable operations.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, Wis. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc's Time Warner Cable unit said Monday it has entered an agreement in principle to switch cable television systems in Wisconsin and Indiana with  Marcus Cable.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Time Warner will receive about 55,000 customers and Marcus Cable will receive about 70,000 customers.</p>
<p>The trade typifies the long-term strategies of both companies, with Time Warner receiving customers in larger metropolitan markets, while Marcus Cable receives customers that fit into its stand alone cable system clusters, the companies said.</p>
<p>Time Warner shares were up 1/4 at 43-1/4 Monday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
